{%- comment -%}
  snippets/ds-cart-agreement.liquid — License-terms consent gate.

  Brutalist checkbox + link to /pages/license. The user must check the
  box before any [name="checkout"] button on the page becomes clickable.
  Establishes click-wrap consent (stronger than browse-wrap per the
  Society of Fonts EULA enforceability analysis).

  Rendered in two places:
    1. Cart drawer footer (via snippets/ds-cart-summary.liquid)
    2. Full cart page (via sections/main-cart.liquid, above the cart
       summary block)

  Behavior
    • Consent state persists in sessionStorage for the duration of the
      visitor's session — re-checking required after the browser closes.
    • Inline JS is guarded by window.__dsCartAgreementInit so it only
      attaches listeners once, even if the snippet renders twice on the
      cart page (drawer + page summary).
    • Sync runs on initial load and on every Horizon `cart:update` event
      (fired after cart morphs), so the checkbox + button state stay
      consistent even after add/remove actions.
    • Both checkboxes (drawer + cart page) share the same sessionStorage
      key, so checking either one unlocks the Checkout button in both.

  Known limitation
    • Shopify-rendered dynamic checkout buttons (Apple Pay, Shop Pay
      Express, Google Pay, PayPal Express) submit directly to Shopify
      and bypass this gate. If affirmative consent is critical, disable
      dynamic checkout buttons in Settings → Payments. Standard email
      checkout flow is fully gated.
    • CSS lives in sections/ds-header.liquid alongside the existing
      ds-cart styling. Loaded on every page via the header section
      group, so it applies on the cart page too.
{%- endcomment -%}

<label class="ds-cart__agreement">
  <input
    type="checkbox"
    class="ds-cart__agreement-input"
    data-ds-cart-agreement
    aria-describedby="ds-cart-agreement-text"
  >
  <span class="ds-cart__agreement-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="ds-cart__agreement-text" id="ds-cart-agreement-text">
    I agree to the
    <a
      href="/pages/license"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener"
      class="ds-cart__agreement-link"
    >License terms</a>
  </span>
</label>

{%- comment -%}
  The gating script for [data-ds-cart-agreement] lives in
  sections/ds-header.liquid (with the rest of the cart-drawer logic)
  so it runs from the initial document parse. Inline scripts that
  arrive later via cart-drawer morphing don't re-execute, which is
  what was breaking the initial disabled state on the Checkout
  button. The header-level script also runs a MutationObserver so
  the gate stays correct across every subsequent morph.
{%- endcomment -%}
